                        "sense_id": "143a33b2-caa5-318a-abc5-295423823b68",
                        "entry_id": "2044d086-0439-3345-8492-61ad279d3c16",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large grey European goose, Anser anser, with pink legs and dull orange beak."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0770507e-f209-4672-aa50-5edce1b1f13c",
                                "sense_id": "143a33b2-caa5-318a-abc5-295423823b68",
                                "text": "Since the war, migrant greylags have virtually deserted the Duddon estuary, so it is a source of great satisfaction that the WAGBI greylags have taken to roosting on the sands in mid-winter, flighting to and from the reserve."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c61a389-8e6c-461f-a528-8970228b2760",
                                "sense_id": "143a33b2-caa5-318a-abc5-295423823b68",
                                "text": "Greylags used to concentrate on British estuaries, eating roots of rushes and sedges, as they do in other parts of their range."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a35456f-3d06-4f6d-821b-b9950d5ab6d9",
                                "sense_id": "143a33b2-caa5-318a-abc5-295423823b68",
                                "text": "Earlier, 250 more had flown to Rattray beach, nearly all pinkfeet although I saw four greylags and heard others."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
